1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,040
When Sonja Detrinidad opened her online shop selling houseplants, she didn’t have high hopes for it.
索尼娅·德特里尼达开网店卖室内绿植时，对它并没有抱太大希望。

2
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:14,882
But the opposite happened: She was flooded, shipping out 1,200 orders in June of 2020 alone.
但结果恰恰相反：订单如潮水般涌来，仅2020年6月一个月她就发出了1200份订单。

3
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:19,742
In the past year, Detrinidad sent out more than 70,000 plants.
在过去一年里，德特里尼达卖出了7万多盆植物。

4
00:00:20,542 --> 00:00:26,792
Her success is just one example of increased time at home leading to an explosion in the houseplant industry.
她的成功只是一个例子，说明居家时间增多引发了室内植物行业的爆发式增长。

5
00:00:27,592 --> 00:00:33,502
“Plants are in fashion right now,” says Dr. Melinda Knuth, a researcher from the University of Florida.
“植物现在很流行，”佛罗里达大学的研究员梅林达·努斯博士说。

6
00:00:34,302 --> 00:00:39,642
“People who live in plant-rich environments report a higher life satisfaction rating,” she says.
“生活在绿植丰富环境中的人，报告的生活满意度更高，”她说。

7
00:00:40,442 --> 00:00:44,412
“Adding more nature to our environment can change our mood and how we think.”
“给我们的环境增添更多自然元素，可以改变我们的情绪和思维方式。”

8
00:00:45,212 --> 00:00:53,002
Plants can improve our state of mind in a few ways but the biggest is by decreasing our level of cortisol, the stress hormone in our body.
植物可以从几个方面改善我们的精神状态，但最主要的一点是降低体内的压力激素——皮质醇的水平。

9
00:00:53,802 --> 00:01:00,692
“Students who are around plants perform better academically than students who are in a classroom without plants,” says Knuth.
“身边有植物的学生，学习成绩比在没有植物的教室里的学生更好，”努斯说。

10
00:01:01,492 --> 00:01:05,242
“This productivity also translates into the workplace for adults.
“对成年人来说，这种效率的提升同样体现在工作场所。

11
00:01:06,042 --> 00:01:11,922
Our study showed that there was a 30% decrease in sick leave for people who were in plant-rich workplaces.”
我们的研究表明，在绿植丰富的工作场所，人们的病假减少了30%。”

12
00:01:12,722 --> 00:01:22,942
If you’re among the groups of people who are enjoying the mental and physical health benefits of surrounding yourself with plants, don’t beat yourself up if one (or a few!) doesn’t make it.
如果你也属于那些正在享受被植物环绕所带来的身心健康益处的人，那么当一盆（或几盆！）没养活时，不要责怪自己。

13
00:01:23,742 --> 00:01:30,412
“Doctors practice medicine and lawyers practice law and you should allow yourself the practice it takes to sustain a plant.
“医生要行医，律师要从事法律工作，你也应该允许自己经历养活一株植物所需的练习。

14
00:01:31,212 --> 00:01:34,642
Tending to plants is an exercise in patience and learning.
照料植物是一种关于耐心和学习的锻炼。

15
00:01:35,442 --> 00:01:40,872
Be invested in taking care of it, but if it dies, go get another one,” Detrinidad says.
用心照顾它，但如果它死了，就再去买一盆，”德特里尼达说。
